{
  "id": "COMPOUND:43279 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanism by which Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3α)- interacts with SCCH-26 through a series of target-mediated pathways. The compound is identified as a target of multiple entities, including the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is itself a target of several compounds, including WS-5995 B and 5α,6α-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3β,7α-diol. These entities are all linked to SCCH-26, indicating a possible pathway where Spirostan-3,27-diol, (3α)- acts as a modulator of the proteasome regulatory subunit 14, which in turn influences SCCH-26. The presence of multiple targets and their shared interaction with SCCH-26 suggests a potential role in modulating cellular processes, possibly through the regulation of proteasome activity. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between the compound and SCCH-26, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
